-- title:
--   Liftable level-two value at a maximal ideal of B
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q\ge 5$, a valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, a field $k$ of characteristic $q$ with decidable equality, and a ring homomorphism $\mathrm{red}\colon A\to k$. Let $a\in k$ lie in `ssJSet q k`, i.e. every elliptic Weierstrass curve over $k$ with $j$-invariant $a$ has no nonzero point killed by $q$; assume $a^{q^2}=a$ and $a=0$ or $a=1728$. Let $K/\mathbb Q$ be a finite intermediate field of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, write $A_0=A\cap K$ for `coeffSubring A K` and $\mathrm{red}_0$ for the induced map $A_0\to k$, and let $\varpi\in A_0$ be such that $\ker\mathrm{red}_0$ is exactly the set of multiples of $\varpi$. Let $l\in k$ satisfy $a\,(16l)^2(16l-1)^2=256\bigl((16l)^2-16l+1\bigr)^3$ and let $y\in A_0$ reduce to $l$. Let $B$ be a subring of the Laurent series over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ consisting precisely of those $z$ lying in `lambdaFieldOver q K` — the subfield generated by the constant series from $K$ together with $\lambda$ and its $q$-fold $q$-expansion $\lambda_q$ — which are integral over the image, under the doubling operator `qExpand _ 2`, of the subring $R_0$ of Laurent series of the form $r(j,j_q)/s(j,j_q)$ with $r,s\in A_0[X_0,X_1]$ and $s(a,a^q)\neq 0$ (here $j_q$ is the $q$-fold $q$-expansion of $j$); $R_0$ is assumed Noetherian and local. Then for every maximal ideal $Q$ of $B$ there are $l'\in k$ with $a\,(16l')^2(16l'-1)^2=256\bigl((16l')^2-16l'+1\bigr)^3$ and $y'\in A_0$ reducing to $l'$ such that any element of $B$ whose underlying Laurent series is the constant series $\varpi$, or $\lambda-y'$, or $\lambda_q-y'^{\,q}$ (each written through `lambdaEval`), lies in $Q$; the three assertions are implications, so they do not themselves claim that these series belong to $B$.
--
--   This is the residue computation at a maximal ideal of the level-two normalisation $B$ over a supersingular node $(a,a^q)$ with $a\in\{0,1728\}$: the contraction of $Q$ forces $\varpi\in Q$, and the level-two relation pins the residue of $\lambda$ down to a value liftable to $A_0$, with $\lambda_q$ congruent to the $q$-th power of that lift. It feeds [`ModularCurve.LambdaNodeLocalized.exists_eq_comap_maximalIdeal_lambdaLocalizedAtPoint_of_isMaximal`](thm.html#ModularCurve.LambdaNodeLocalized.exists_eq_comap_maximalIdeal_lambdaLocalizedAtPoint_of_isMaximal), the step identifying maximal ideals of $B$ with those of the $\lambda$-localisation at a node.
-- source:
